Skill	craft:github
Bash	cd <work>; cat <craft>/skills/github/take-in.md; git remote -v; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -5; ls
Bash	cd <work>; bash <craft>/skills/github/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"; cat README.md; git log --oneline
Bash	cd <work>; gh issue view 91 --json title,body 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"; gh repo view --json nameWithOwner 2>&1
text	The README's install command reads `npm instal shop`, which fails because npm has no `instal` command. I'll correct it to `npm install shop`.  
Bash	cd <craft>/skills/github; sed -n 1,200p tracker.md; ls scripts
Bash	cd <work>; D=<craft>/skills/github; gh label list 2>&1 | head; bash $D/scripts/collect.sh take-in 91 bug,debt README.md "npm instal" install 2>&1 | tail -5
Bash	cat <tmp>/collect.KYSM1r
text	The tracker has no duplicates, no neighbours and no linked work. Next I make the worktree.
Bash	cd <work>; bash <craft>/skills/github/scripts/worktree.sh 91 docs/91-fix-install-command 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"
ToolSearch	
EnterWorktree	
Bash	sed -i '' 's/npm instal shop/npm install shop/' README.md && git diff; ls -a; grep -rn "instal\b" . --exclude-dir=.git
text	The repository has no check command: it has no `package.json` and no `Makefile`. The closest check is a search for the wrong word, and it finds no other `instal`. Now the review.
Skill	craft:review-loop
Bash	git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: correct the install command in the README" && git log --oneline -2 && git merge-base origin/main HEAD
Agent	Review README docs change
subBash	git diff 6cef989..HEAD && git ls-files
Bash	gh pr list --state merged --limit 5 --json title 2>&1; gh repo view acme/shop --json visibility --jq .visibility; grep -rn "instal\b" . --exclude-dir=.git; echo "grep exit=$?"; git push -u origin HEAD 2>&1 | tail -2
Bash	cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; Closes #91; ; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so that command failed. The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Correct the install command in the README from `npm instal shop` to `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** worth check skipped (documents only). ponytail-review skipped (documents only, and not installed). Walk skipped (documents only). Round 1: one review subagent on `6cef989..ba7aa47`, 0 findings. No architecture file or ADR folder: `craft:architecture` can write the first one. Codex read skipped (a README is not a skill, a prompt or a spec). Last pass and security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command; the closest check, a search for `instal`, finds no other match.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none beyond the task.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** README.md is the change itself.; EOF; gh pr create --base main --head docs/91-fix-install-command --title "docs: correct the install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md --assignee @me 2>&1; gh issue edit 91 --add-assignee @me 2>&1 | tail -1
text	I fixed the README for **#91 README: the install command says npm instal** and pushed the branch, but I could not open the pull request: `gh pr create` failed.  **What is done** - **Take-in:** the check printed `take #91`. The tracker has no duplicates, no open bug or debt issues on the same code, and no linked work. - **Branch and worktree:** `docs/91-fix-install-command`, made by `worktree.sh`. The issue is assigned to you and has the label `in progress`. - **Change:** `README.md:3` now says `npm install shop` instead of `npm instal shop`. Commit `ba7aa47 docs: correct the install command in the README`, with no `Co-Authored-By:` trailer, as your instructions say. - **Review:** documents only, so one round. One review subagent read `6cef989..ba7aa47` and found nothing. Because the change is documents only, there was no Codex read, no last pass and no security review. The repository has no architecture file, so `craft:architecture` can write the first one. - **Check:** the repository has no check command (no `package.json`, no `Makefile`). As the closest check, I searched the repository for `instal`, and there is no other match. - **Push:** the branch is on `origin`.  **What failed** `gh pr create` returned `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. The `gh` in this environment is a stub, and it has no answer for that call. So there is no pull request and I did not ask the merge question. The pull request description, with its `## Review` section, is in `/tmp/pr91.md`. To open it with a real `gh`:  ```bash gh pr create --base main --head docs/91-fix-install-command \   --title "docs: correct the install command in the README" \   --body-file /tmp/pr91.md --assignee @me ```  **Docs:** `README.md` is the change itself, so no other documents needed an update.
